                        "entry_id": "8ff1b9b6-79ad-3934-86bb-461055c8e9ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In an immemorial manner, from time immemorial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c78f333-cc4b-4a1d-8bc1-e496c163f237",
                                "sense_id": "e2b2983c-871d-34f0-9b2b-93c53cde6035",
                                "text": "[…] by vast odds, the most terrific of all mortal disasters have immemorially and indiscriminately befallen tens and hundreds of thousands of those who have gone upon the waters […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0f7026f-37b1-46f7-a1af-f6399bec9b99",
                                "sense_id": "e2b2983c-871d-34f0-9b2b-93c53cde6035",
                                "text": "Yet, O reader, the brave woman accepted the lot, and took up the cry which had been its sign immemorially, and which thenceforward was to be her salutation without change—“Unclean, unclean!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b688ebc6-00ca-4c79-a627-de8b2f147765",
                                "sense_id": "e2b2983c-871d-34f0-9b2b-93c53cde6035",
                                "text": "[…] as for barbers, he had never liked those who cut his own hair; he thought too how it would disgust Pundit Jairam to learn that his former pupil had taken up barbering, a profession immemorially low."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
